{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774709,"nonce":"o4SAQBJLxQ0uEFqKDnPgygXryVk=","title":"docs: re-skin on Lucode (shadcn/ui) theme — light-default, edges-only accents","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #7 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/docs-lucode-theme` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-14T17:25:04Z · Merged: 2026-07-14T19:02:53Z\n\n\nThe docs site was dark-first with a solid-emerald active-nav block and Inter — it read as heavy product chrome, not a place to read. This rebases the docs **skin** on the [`lucode-starlight`](https://github.com/lucas-labs/lucode-starlight-theme) plugin (a shadcn/ui-inspired Starlight theme) and layers a thin Scarab identity over it, rather than hand-rolling the theme.\n\nThe control-plane app (SolidJS) keeps its carapace identity — DESIGN.md §1–9 are unchanged. Docs is now documented as its own reading surface in **§10**.\n\n\n- **Light is the default**; dark is Lucode's neutral shadcn dark (not carapace green) — dark deliberately deprioritized for a reading surface.\n- **Green sparingly, at the edges only**: emerald on links / TOC-current / active-nav rail / focus; **copper \"fence brackets\" _are_ the primary CTA** (sharp corner brackets, no fill — a nod to fence-scoped durability); `note` aside emerald, `tip` copper. `caution`/`danger` keep semantic orange/red.\n- **Type: Geist + JetBrains Mono** (drop Inter — Geist is the face shadcn/Lucode is drawn with).\n- **Splash body constrained** to line up with the hero (was full-bleed).\n\n\n- `.entry-link` forced to `height:auto` so long ADR titles wrap instead of overlapping (Lucode caps entries at 30px via an Astro-scoped style).\n- Brand tokens set **unlayered**: Starlight core defines `--sl-color-text-accent` unlayered (its default blue), which outranks `@layer lucode`.\n\n\n- Production build green (51 pages; Lucode + starlight-openapi + schema extension coexist).\n- Checked hero, content pages, asides, and sidebar in both light and dark in the browser.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}